                                               Annex 1

Participant Information Sheet

In this study, you will be asked to participate in a series of assessments during commuting
routes in the Brussels Capital Region (BCR). The experiment will take place from 1:30 to
5:30 pm. In this time, you will alternate between walking and biking along urban bike and
pedestrian routes. You will also be asked to take the tram. Researchers from UCLouvain will
be accompanying you along these urban routes. You will wear non-invasive and non-intrusive
wearable sensors to measure heart-rate variability, skin conductance, skin temperature, together
with EEG (if it is accepted by ethics commission) and eye-tracking glasses and illuminance due
to sunlight. You will also complete brief surveys about your emotional state and your
perceptions of the urban environment. These surveys will be administered at the beginning &
end of each phase before or after biking/walking, to track changes in your physiological
responses and psychological state as you move through different urban settings.

Your participation is entirely voluntary. All information collected will be handled in accordance
with GDPR and the Belgian Law of 30 July 2018 on the protection of individuals with regards
to the processing of personal data. By signing this consent form, you agree to take part in this
study and consent to anonymous statistical analysis of the data you provide. You may withdraw
any or all of your data from the study at any time without consequence. All data will be stored
securely under UCLouvain regulations; see https://www.uclouvain.be/en/privacy for details.

