These questions are designed to collect basic demographic, residential, and behavioral
information that may help contextualize each participant’s responses during the experiment.
The form also captures participants’ physical characteristics relevant to sensor use (e.g., vision
correction and handedness), as well as their mobility habits and familiarity with the study area.
This information will not be used to exclude participants but to aid in the interpretation of
collected psychophysiological data.

