                 B) Survey during the experimental campaign

These surveys include participants’ thermal and psychological perceptual responses to urban
environments during urban commuting. The survey incorporates elements from validated and
shortened standardized questionnaires covering both thermal and psychological dimensions.
These include the Comfort Sensation Vote (CSV) and Thermal Sensation Vote (TSV) for
thermal perception (Xue et al., 2020), the 6-item State-Trait Anxiety Inventory (STAI-6) for
psychological stress (Marteau and Bekker, 1992; Spielberger, 1983), and the 11-item Perceived
Restorativeness Scale (PRS-11) for environmental restoration (Hartig et al., 1997; Pasini et al.,
2014). Additionally, custom-made questions on comfort and environmental pleasantness
(Environmental Stressor and Greenness) have also been included (see complete survey in table
2). The survey will require approximately 4 minutes of time to fill in.

As described in figure 1 the experiment will begin at 1:30 pm and will end at 5:30 pm. UponSurveySurvey Survey
arrival participants will be invited to sit in an air-conditioned room for the signing of the consentSurvey  Survey
form, the installation of the physiological sensors, and the filling in of the ‘participantSurvey
background information’ form and to complete the survey. Then the participants will be asked
to either bike or walk along a predefined path for 30 minutes. Once this is completed, theDebriefing & ConsentWalkSittingWalk
sensors will be checked, and the participants will be asked to fill in the survey. Once this isBackground InformationBikeBike
completed another block of 30 minutes of either biking or walking will follow. Tricycle will beBaseline Data Collection
used for biking having 3 wheels which will prevent accidental fall and ensure safety. Once this
is completed, once again the sensors will be checked, and the participant will be asked to fill in
the survey. These two initial blocks of 30 minutes of biking and walking will take place in
either green or impervious urban environments – choice that will be randomized as it will be
the order on which the participant will walk or bike first. This initial block of data collection
will be followed by a tram route with a total duration of ~30min where the participant will be
sitting in an air-conditioned environment. This will bring the participant back to the initial
location to start block two, which will be organized as block one. Before the following 30
minutes of biking or walking, the participant is asked to fill in the survey once more. Block two
will unfold as per block one after which the participant will have completed the experiment.
Along with the experimental campaign, refreshments will be provided.

