                                             Appendix C
                                  Time period selection for experiment
SOLWEIG (Solar and Long Wave Environmental Irradiance Geometry) model was used to
simulate mean radiant temperature (Tₘᵣₜ) for 2022 to 2024. Human thermal comfort indices -
Physiologically Equivalent Temperature (PET) and Universal Thermal Climate Index (UTCI)
were generated. These were calculated using the Pythermalcomfort library with inputs
including Tmrt, wind speed, relative humidity, and air temperature.
On hourly plot, Tₘᵣₜ peaked at roughly 53.9 °C around midday (when solar radiation is
highest), but PET and UTCI—because they also respond to the slower‐warming air mass and
the cooling effects of wind—peaked later at 15 & 16 hour.
PET and UTCI values are elevated between 2:00 pm and 5:00 pm. To capture this peak period
while allowing time for consent and preparation, participants are asked to arrive at 1:30 pm.
Therefore, the experimental window was set from 1:30 pm to 5:30 pm.

